  "preamble": "The loss or elision of the lateral consonant /l/, often in syllable-final position or in specific clusters. In Southern Tsakonian, [l] was deleted before back and central vowels (λόγος > όγο), while Northern Tsakonian keeps it.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Elision, L-dropping",
